  "_comment": "The original blockarcanefurnace dropped itself for every one of its eleven metadata - 0 the base plate, 1-9 the shell of the 3x3x3, 10 the nozzle - with the metadata kept on the dropped stack. 1.21.1 has no implicit self-drop, so the drop is data: one block_state_property-gated pool per variant (D-001: variant 0 = metadata 0, variant 1 = metadata 10, variants 2..10 = metadata 1..9), each setting the minecraft:block_state component so the drop keeps its variant - a shell cell that drops a base plate loses the grid position its faces were published from, and a nozzle that drops a plate loses the eject direction the whole furnace depends on (TC-M4-06-m, t_42864caf). An unconditional pool would fire for every state and duplicate the drop, so each pool is gated.",
